<!--
    Kuna #1793: "A stack slot passed as an out-parameter is read back through
    a variable that is never assigned"
    https://github.com/Noelo-Lab/kuna/issues/1793

    Hand-assembled Windows x64 (GNU as, Intel syntax).  outslot is the
    reporter's 80-byte blob: with rsp at entry-0x28, lea r9,[rsp+0x60] passes
    the incoming stack slot at entry+0x38 as fill's out-parameter, and the slot
    is loaded again after the call:

        lea  r9,[rsp+0x60]        ; &slot
        call fill                 ; fill: mov [r9],rcx
        mov  rcx,[rsp+0x60]       ; the value fill wrote
        mov  rax,[rcx]
        call QWORD PTR [rax+0x8]

    outslot_init clears the slot first (mov QWORD PTR [rsp+0x60],0), and
    outslot_loop refills an entry+0x38 slot through rdx on every iteration
    (store: mov [rdx],rcx) and sums it.  outparam passes the first stack
    argument slot, entry+0x28, which the prototype takes as a parameter.
    outpair sets two adjacent ints with one 8-byte store and passes each by
    address; outindex also indexes the slot's address.  Neither is one scalar
    object, and both keep their storage references.

    Stage model: P6 variable naming.  ScopeLocal::restructure leaves the
    prototype's parameter range to the parameter symbols, and entry+0x38 is
    not one (the slots at 0x28 and 0x30 are unused), so it had no symbol: the
    reference printed as raw storage while the load printed as v2, declared
    and never assigned, and outslot_init read v2 = NULL; ... *v2:

        fill(a0,0,0x10,&Stack0000000000000038)
        v1 = *(code **)(*v2 + 8);

    kuna_paramareaslot.rs (always on) maps such an address-taken slot as a
    local once the prototype is final, so the reference and the accesses
    share one name.  The parameter slot in outparam keeps its parameter.
    Mapping outpair's 8 bytes as one local printed the second address as
    &((char *)Register00000020)[0x3c], and mapping outindex's slot indexed
    an 8-byte scalar, ((int8 *)&v1)[a1].
-->
